    "scripture": "Exodus 31:3-5",
    "text": "And I have filled him with the spirit of God, in wisdom, and in understanding, and in knowledge, and in all manner of workmanship, to devise cunning works, to work in gold, and in silver, and in brass, and in cutting of stones, to set them, and in carving of timber, to work in all manner of workmanship.",
    "principle": "God filled Bezalel with His Spirit specifically for creative work. Not administration. Not prophecy. Not warfare. ART. The first person Scripture names as Spirit-filled was an artist. Beauty is not secondary to the Kingdom — it is integral. Bezalel designs because God designed first, and design is worship."
  },

